WHAT THIS DELTA IS, AFTER D-153
-------------------------------
It contains EXACTLY ONE thing: the hS byte pin — a module constant carrying an
unsubstitutable sentinel, plus the single test that checks it.

Everything the pre-D-153 version of this delta carried has MOVED into the
pre-derivation candidate as a reviewed code change (D-153 A2, work order W1):
the rename to test_differential_self_test_all_governed_packs, the chain-derived
corpus totals, and the presence-conditional non-authenticating successor shape
assertion. None of those depends on a digest, so none of them belongs in a
post-window commit.

WHY THE SPLIT IS FORCED (D-153 finding 3, the published-head-suite trap)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The mint ALONE reddens the old literal 9/99 corpus assertions. If the cure for
that redness lived in the fixation commit, the suite would be red across the
whole window — the same defect O-1-E was killed for. So every digest-INDEPENDENT
consequence of the chain read must land BEFORE derivation, where it is green in
both coordinates; only hS, which is unknowable before the mint, may wait.

THE ONE BENCH SUBSTITUTION
--------------------------
SUCCESSOR_PINSET_SHA256 ships as "S0-FIXATION-SUBSTITUTION-PENDING". It is not
64 hex characters on purpose: an unsubstituted delta fails loudly on the guard
assertion instead of silently pinning a plausible-looking value (a 64-zero
placeholder would not have that property). The runsheet substitutes the minted
digest mechanically and proves the sentinel is gone.

WHY hS MUST BE A LITERAL AND CANNOT BE DERIVED
----------------------------------------------
It is the byte authenticator for the successor allowlist class. A test that
derived the digest from the file it is checking would recompute to whatever a
tampered file now hashes to and would authenticate nothing. D-151 condition 2
forbids the shape assertions from standing in for it, and the shape method says
so in its own docstring.

VERIFIED BEFORE PUBLICATION OF THIS DELTA
-----------------------------------------
  * `git apply --check` clean against tests/test_receipt_histsem.py at the
    branch head (i.e. against the post-W1 candidate).
  * The candidate suite is green in BOTH coordinates WITHOUT this delta
    applied — pre-mint (shape assertion vacuous) and post-mint against a REAL
    synthetic minted successor. That is the D-153 W1/D4 verification, and it is
    what proves this delta carries nothing the candidate already needs.

